WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.125
DAB builds on the Information Bottleneck framework
but replaces its rate term with an

00:00:04.205 --> 00:00:08.329
achievable rate borrowed from rate-distortion
theory with finite cardinality.

00:00:08.409 --> 00:00:12.534
Concretely,

00:00:12.614 --> 00:00:16.738
the model learns a codebook of centroid
distributions that quantize the encoders of all training points.

00:00:16.818 --> 00:00:20.943
The uncertainty of a new example is simply its
expected statistical distance,

00:00:21.023 --> 00:00:25.147
here the Kullback-Leibler divergence, from that codebook.

00:00:25.227 --> 00:00:29.352
Training alternates between gradient updates of the
encoder and decoder and cheap analytic

00:00:29.432 --> 00:00:33.556
updates of the soft assignments and centroids,

00:00:33.636 --> 00:00:37.761
echoing the classic Blahut-Arimoto algorithm.

00:00:37.841 --> 00:00:41.965
The result is closely analogous to a Gaussian Process,

00:00:42.045 --> 00:00:46.170
where the codebook plays the role of inducing
points and statistical distance replaces Euclidean distance.
